Item 05 is done, in 17 minutes of wall clock against the 3-hour cap. Nothing was run in the background, nothing was committed, and nothing was written to `solutions/`.

**What was built.** `learning/cost_model.py` predicts log10 nodes to refute optimum − 1 from label-free graph features. Censored counts enter a hand-written Tobit likelihood, since neither survival library is installed. The design is linear in n times density, ratio, optimum fraction, degree, treewidth, degeneracy and components, plus §16's drift term, with a LightGBM residual correction on scale-free features. Model selection used fit at n ≤ 60 scored at 75, so the test sizes were touched once.

**The result.** Trained at 10–75, the chosen model puts 87.8% of the 98 default counts and 89.3% of the 103 pre-fix csearch counts at 100–125 within one decade. The §11 cell law reaches 58–65% and the §14 surface 59–61%. The kill criterion is not met for the chosen model, and is met for the linear Tobit alone at 73%. The bias is +0.4 decades, so it over-predicts. The single failing class is the generated 100-customer d = 2 cell, which is 96% decomposable. Without it the 100 band is 57 of 58 within a decade. The relabelling noise floor is 30–100× below the error.

**The recertify entries.** The five finished entries are predicted to MAE 0.38 with bias +0.38, all within a decade, with Spearman 0.4 on their order. The three still open have run 63 hours and have visited at least 10^11.49 nodes. Cheapest-first order for them:

1. `Random-125-125-2-5_0`, predicted 10^11.15, already past its prediction
2. `Random-125-125-2-3_0`, predicted 10^11.34, already past its prediction
3. `Random-125-125-2-2_0`, predicted 10^11.85, the most expensive of the eight by every model

**A side finding.** In all 70 upward cells where Theorem 2 is on, §18's post-fix counts differ from the §16 run's counts, so the whole §16 run is pre-fix. That let the csearch model train on the 50–75 data. All predictions are for the pre-fix search. Post-fix ridge counts at 100 are at least 15× larger and the model has never seen one at 125.

**Files.** Report §19 appended to `reports/ml_nature.md`, tables in `reports/cost_model_tables.md`, predictions and the recertify table under `learning/data/ensemble/`, nine tests in `tests/test_cost_model.py`. The full suite passes: 917 passed, 2 skipped, 1 xfailed in 79 s. PROGRESS.md has the iteration 5 entry and reads 5/14 solved. The item is ticked in `iterations.md`. Nine items remain, so LOOP_COMPLETE was not added.

